 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The fine print</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What Myrtle Beach golf community buyers miss</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.8rem;margin:1.2rem 0 0;padding:0;max-width:760px"><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Transfer fees ride with the deed, not the listing.</strong> At Barefoot, a resale that carries a golf membership means a $2,750 transfer fee and a 60-day enrollment window after closing. Ask what obligations attach to the specific lot before you offer, not at the closing table.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The Intracoastal view can carry a flood premium.</strong> Waterway-adjacent pockets of Grande Dunes, Barefoot, and Arrowhead can sit in FEMA Zone AE, where lenders require flood insurance. The fairway lots a street inland often do not. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">coastal insurance guide</a> covers what that costs; we pull the flood zone on every golf lot we show.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">A public course means no membership obligation.</strong> Public-course communities like Blackmoor pair a Gary Player design with a $35 monthly HOA and no club dues at all. Clients of ours owned a home in Blackmoor, then sold it and bought in Seasons at Prince Creek West, a 55+ community a few minutes away. That side is covered on our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">55+ communities page</a>.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Second-home rules still apply on the fairway.</strong> A golf villa you use part-time is a second home or investment property to the county and the lender: the 6 percent tax rate, second-home loan occupancy rules, and rental restrictions all still run. The math is in our <a href="/buyers/second-home/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">second home guide</a> and <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax calculator</a>.</span></li></ul></div></section>
 
